            <div xml:id="d411">

                <pb facs="0658" n="546" sameAs="frus:frus1907p1/pg546"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 2160.</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The British Ambassador to
                        the Secretary of State</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >British Embassy</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1906-11-06"><hi rendition="#italic">November 6,
                        1906</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 208.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: On June 23 I had the honor of leaving at
                    the State Department a memorandum respecting the leasing to the British North
                    Borneo Company of certain small islands off the coast of Borneo.</p>
                <p>I have now received a dispatch from His Majesty’s secretary of state for foreign
                    affairs, inquiring what progress has been made in the matter, and accordingly I
                    have the honor to ask you to be so good as to inform me whether it has yet been
                    found possible to come to any decision as to the proposals set forth in the
                    memorandum referred to above.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">H. M. Durand.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
